+## Bundled FFmpeg media tools
+
+`npm run build:media` builds ffmpeg/ffprobe/ffplay from the pinned official source `ffmpeg-9.0.2.tar.xz` (SHA256 `8c3850283eb25fa026482078a04051e0be17347b09ef81a0849bec15a96e002e`, `https://ffmpeg.org/releases/`) with an LGPL-only configuration (`--disable-gpl --disable-nonfree --disable-version3 --disable-autodetect --disable-network`, verified against `-buildconf` output). The staged binaries live in `scope-extension/resources/bin/darwin-<arch>/` next to the device service and dynamically link the bundled `libSDL2-2.0.0.dylib` (sdl2-compat, zlib-style license) and `libSDL3.dylib` (SDL3, zlib-style license; loaded by sdl2-compat via `dlopen`). FFmpeg 9.0.2 is LGPL-2.1-or-later in this configuration: the build uses dynamic linking for its bundled dylib dependencies, and `scope-extension/resources/licenses/ffmpeg/` carries the LGPL-2.1 license text, the SDL license texts, the exact source tarball, the build recipe (`build-media.cjs` + `BUILD-RECIPE.txt`), and build metadata — included for review; whether the corresponding-source obligation is fully satisfied remains a release-time review item. Only the macOS host build exists; Windows/Linux packaging is not implemented. Binaries are ad-hoc signed for local use — release signing, notarization and a complete license clearance remain release-time work, and this inventory is not legal approval. Evidence: `docs/0.1.3/evidence/media-bundle.md`.
